1
00:00:00,260 --> 00:00:02,965
For three months, I didn't lift a

2
00:00:02,965 --> 00:00:04,481
single weight.

3
00:00:04,481 --> 00:00:06,360
Not one push-up.

4
00:00:06,481 --> 00:00:08,644
I lost four kilos.

5
00:00:08,744 --> 00:00:10,771
My t-shirts got loose.

6
00:00:10,871 --> 00:00:14,255
My bench press dropped by twenty kilos.

7
00:00:14,376 --> 00:00:17,949
Everyone told me, you're starting from zero.

8
00:00:18,071 --> 00:00:19,039
Zero?

9
00:00:19,039 --> 00:00:20,844
Like, zero zero?

10
00:00:20,965 --> 00:00:23,371
But then something strange happened.

11
00:00:23,471 --> 00:00:24,786
When I came back,

12
00:00:24,786 --> 00:00:28,349
everything came back faster than anyone expected.

13
00:00:28,449 --> 00:00:29,786
Stay till the end,

14
00:00:29,786 --> 00:00:32,081
because the reason is the coolest thing

15
00:00:32,081 --> 00:00:33,571
your body does.

16
00:00:33,692 --> 00:00:34,865
Week two.

17
00:00:34,965 --> 00:00:36,981
Here's the first surprise.

18
00:00:37,081 --> 00:00:38,734
For the first two weeks,

19
00:00:38,734 --> 00:00:40,918
I lost almost nothing.

20
00:00:42,197 --> 00:00:44,607
Strength holds on for about two to

21
00:00:44,607 --> 00:00:45,834
three weeks.

22
00:00:45,934 --> 00:00:47,518
Muscle size too.

23
00:00:47,639 --> 00:00:50,107
What I lost first was the pump.

24
00:00:50,207 --> 00:00:51,913
My muscles looked flat,

25
00:00:51,913 --> 00:00:53,965
because they were holding less water and

26
00:00:53,965 --> 00:00:55,602
less stored energy.

27
00:00:55,702 --> 00:00:58,171
The muscle itself was still there.

28
00:00:58,292 --> 00:01:00,876
So your muscles were just deflated?

29
00:01:00,945 --> 00:01:02,024
Exactly.

30
00:01:02,114 --> 00:01:04,008
Like a balloon with less air,

31
00:01:04,008 --> 00:01:05,656
not a smaller balloon.

32
00:01:05,777 --> 00:01:06,919
Month one.

33
00:01:07,019 --> 00:01:08,461
After about a month,

34
00:01:08,461 --> 00:01:10,182
the real drop started.

35
00:01:10,282 --> 00:01:12,014
My bench went down.

36
00:01:12,114 --> 00:01:13,687
Push-ups felt heavy.

37
00:01:14,966 --> 00:01:17,987
Then, slowly, the muscle itself started to

38
00:01:17,987 --> 00:01:18,856
shrink.

39
00:01:18,977 --> 00:01:20,235
Month three.

40
00:01:20,335 --> 00:01:22,072
I looked in the mirror and barely

41
00:01:22,072 --> 00:01:23,593
recognised myself.

42
00:01:23,693 --> 00:01:25,456
Four kilos down.

43
00:01:25,556 --> 00:01:26,961
Smaller arms.

44
00:01:27,061 --> 00:01:28,445
Flatter chest.

45
00:01:29,724 --> 00:01:31,761
I thought it was gone for good.

46
00:01:33,514 --> 00:01:34,856
The secret.

47
00:01:34,903 --> 00:01:36,808
Your muscle has a memory,

48
00:01:36,808 --> 00:01:39,235
and it's stored inside the cells.

49
00:01:39,356 --> 00:01:42,093
When you train, your muscle fibres grow,

50
00:01:42,093 --> 00:01:44,703
and they collect extra control centres called

51
00:01:44,703 --> 00:01:45,666
nuclei.

52
00:01:45,766 --> 00:01:47,772
Think of them as tiny builders.

53
00:01:47,893 --> 00:01:50,266
When you stop, the fibres shrink.

54
00:01:50,366 --> 00:01:52,861
But research suggests many of those builders

55
00:01:52,861 --> 00:01:55,319
stay behind, maybe for years.

56
00:01:55,440 --> 00:01:57,829
So the builders just sit there,

57
00:01:57,829 --> 00:01:58,708
waiting?

58
00:01:58,829 --> 00:02:00,529
Waiting for the next order.

59
00:02:00,629 --> 00:02:02,829
That's why a comeback is much faster

60
00:02:02,829 --> 00:02:04,056
than the first time.

61
00:02:04,177 --> 00:02:05,329
The comeback.

62
00:02:05,429 --> 00:02:06,629
So I went back.

63
00:02:06,629 --> 00:02:07,708
Half the weight.

64
00:02:07,724 --> 00:02:08,940
Three days a week.

65
00:02:10,219 --> 00:02:12,277
Week one, everything hurt.

66
00:02:12,377 --> 00:02:14,529
Week two, the pump was back.

67
00:02:14,650 --> 00:02:16,808
Week four, my bench was almost where

68
00:02:16,808 --> 00:02:17,677
I left it.

69
00:02:17,777 --> 00:02:19,272
Muscle that took me a year to

70
00:02:19,272 --> 00:02:21,424
build came back in about a month.

71
00:02:21,545 --> 00:02:23,235
And here's the crazy part.

72
00:02:23,335 --> 00:02:25,419
In one study, one group trained for

73
00:02:25,419 --> 00:02:26,803
six months straight.

74
00:02:26,903 --> 00:02:28,619
The other group took three weeks off,

75
00:02:28,619 --> 00:02:29,972
every six weeks.

76
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:33,124
At the end, both groups had about

77
00:02:33,124 --> 00:02:35,024
the same muscle and strength.

78
00:02:35,145 --> 00:02:37,108
So breaks are free?

79
00:02:37,229 --> 00:02:38,672
Short breaks almost are.

80
00:02:38,672 --> 00:02:40,229
Long breaks cost you,

81
00:02:40,229 --> 00:02:41,903
but you get it back much faster

82
00:02:41,903 --> 00:02:42,877
than you think.

83
00:02:42,998 --> 00:02:44,345
If you have to stop,

84
00:02:44,345 --> 00:02:45,714
keep your protein high,

85
00:02:45,714 --> 00:02:47,440
do a few push-ups or squats once

86
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:49,314
a week, and when you come back,

87
00:02:49,314 --> 00:02:50,866
start at half the weight.

88
00:02:50,987 --> 00:02:52,845
Have you ever had to stop training?

89
00:02:52,861 --> 00:02:54,324
Tell me how long in the comments.
